@Article{	  becht2018,
  abstract	= {A benchmarking analysis on single-cell RNA-seq and mass cytometry data reveals the best-performing technique for dimensionality reduction.},
  annote	= {Paper that compares visualization techniques for scRNA-seq data and shows UMAP performs best.
		  
		  An interesting comparison was performed by computing the NMI of a random forest classier on reduced dimensions versus Phenograph clustering. On 3 out of 4 datasets no visualization method had a higher NMI than 0.5 showing that visualization dimensions are not sufficiently informative of cell heterogeneity (t-SNE should not be used for clustering).
		  
		  UMAP was also more robust to subsampling especially compared to t-SNE.
		  
		  Overall there is not much new information in this paper... except a few interesting evaluation methods.},
